-- title:
--   Windowed Iwasawa factorisation for induced sections on GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, and let $\alpha$ denote the idelic modulus: the homomorphism from the ideles $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ to $\mathbb{R}^\times$ obtained from the distributive Haar character of $\mathbb{A}_F$ through $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\to\mathbb{R}$, assumed positive on every idele (hypothesis $h\alpha$). Assume given $c\in[0,\infty]$ with $c\neq\infty$ satisfying the Iwasawa disintegration hypothesis $hc$: for all measurable fundamental domains $D,D'$ for the subgroup of principal ideles (the image of $F^\times$) in $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ with its Haar measure, and every measurable $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to[0,\infty]$ invariant under left translation by the subgroup generated by the rational centre, the rational diagonal torus $\mathrm{diag}(\cdot,1)$ and the adelic unipotent radical, the lower integral of $f$ over the orbit quotient with its quotient measure equals $c$ times $\int_D\int_{D'}\int_{\mathbf K} f(z\cdot\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\cdot k)\,\|t\|^{-1}$, where $z$ acts as a central scalar, $\mathbf K$ is the adelic maximal compact subgroup with its Haar measure, and $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm. Fix such $D,D'$ (measurable, fundamental domains), characters $\mu,\nu,\mu',\nu':(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ that are unitary (absolute value $1$ everywhere) and trivial on principal ideles, complex parameters $s,s'$, and continuous $\varphi,\varphi':\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$ satisfying the induced-section relation $\varphi(bg)=\chi_1(b_{11})\chi_2(b_{22})\varphi(g)$ for $b$ in the adelic Borel subgroup, with $(\chi_1,\chi_2)=(\mu\alpha^{s+1/2},\nu\alpha^{-(s+1/2)})$ for $\varphi$ and $(\mu'\alpha^{s'+1/2},\nu'\alpha^{-(s'+1/2)})$ for $\varphi'$. Finally let $a>0$, $b\in\mathbb{R}$ and let $I\subseteq\mathbb{R}$ be measurable with $\int_{I\cap(0,\infty)} y^{\operatorname{Re}s+\operatorname{Re}s'-1}\,dy<\infty$. Then the function on the quotient sending a class $q$, through a chosen representative $q.\mathrm{out}$, to $\mathbf 1_{\{\|\det g\|\in[a,b]\}}(q.\mathrm{out})\,\mathbf 1_I(\mathrm{ht}(q.\mathrm{out}))\,\varphi(q.\mathrm{out})\overline{\varphi'(q.\mathrm{out})}$, with $\mathrm{ht}$ the adelic height, is integrable for the quotient measure, and its integral equals $c$ (as a real number) times $\int_{\mathbf K}\varphi(k)\overline{\varphi'(k)}\,dk$ times $$\int_D\int_{D'}\chi_1(zt)\chi_2(z)\overline{\chi_1'(zt)\chi_2'(z)}\;\mathbf 1_{[a,b]}\bigl(\|z\|^2\|t\|\bigr)\,\mathbf 1_I\bigl(\|t\|\bigr)\,\|t\|^{-1}.$$
--
--   This is the Iwasawa-coordinate computation of the inner product of two Borel-induced sections over the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ by rational torus times adelic unipotent, with the determinant norm confined to $[a,b]$ and the adelic height confined to an arbitrary measurable window $I$ subject only to a convergence condition; the central and torus variables separate from the compact variable. It feeds the truncated inner-product and Maass–Selberg computations for pseudo-Eisenstein series in the slab region.
